WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:05.220
Trying to read a lot of material during a
busy day can be tough, especially if the material

00:00:05.220 --> 00:00:06.800
is not in your first language.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:11.380
Let’s take a look at a few different techniques
to help you read more but spend less time

00:00:11.380 --> 00:00:12.200
doing it.

00:00:14.710 --> 00:00:19.060
You don’t always have to read articles or
books to improve your reading skills.

00:00:19.060 --> 00:00:23.830
It can be as simple as reading the menu, billboards,
street signs or just reading anything you

00:00:23.830 --> 00:00:25.410
see in English every day.

00:00:25.410 --> 00:00:29.570
If you do enjoy reading, set aside a few minutes
a day to read a book.

00:00:29.570 --> 00:00:33.300
Like anything in life, practice will make
you a better reader.

00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:38.370
Just because you're reading in English, it
doesn’t mean you have to read things you

00:00:38.370 --> 00:00:40.260
have no interest in.

00:00:40.260 --> 00:00:44.320
In fact, reading about something you’re
interested in can speed up your reading and

00:00:44.320 --> 00:00:50.059
understanding of the text, especially as you
may already know a lot about it.

00:00:50.059 --> 00:00:52.250
Think about what you like reading in your
own language.

00:00:52.250 --> 00:00:55.530
For example, do you support a football club?

00:00:55.530 --> 00:00:58.090
You could read their latest match report.

00:00:58.090 --> 00:01:00.809
Do you like to know what the Kardashians are
up to?

00:01:00.809 --> 00:01:03.000
You could read about the latest episode.

00:01:03.989 --> 00:01:07.700
Whatever it is you read, thinking a little
about it or having knowledge of the content

00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:09.100
can help you greatly.

00:01:11.180 --> 00:01:14.820
Sometimes you might not have time to read
everything but you may need to find specific

00:01:14.820 --> 00:01:16.840
information from the text you're reading.

00:01:16.840 --> 00:01:21.820
For example, let’s say you're thinking of
going on holiday to Sydney and you want to

00:01:21.820 --> 00:01:25.060
find out about the weather several months
ahead.

00:01:25.060 --> 00:01:30.020
Using your favourite search engine to look
for a travel page, scan for the keyword, and

00:01:30.020 --> 00:01:32.240
here it will be ‘climate’ or ‘weather’.

00:01:32.240 --> 00:01:35.850
Get to the right section and find the information
you need.

00:01:35.850 --> 00:01:39.650
Make a mental note, or if you're reading a
paper, highlight the area for later.

